

Compilation:
============

1/ Go to src

2/ Use cmake to make the Makefile

cmake ./ 

3/ Compile 

make

Run an Example:
===============

* The directory work, contains a source code t2.cxx , which creates a thermal gas and does the decays making a bunch of histograms

* cd to the directory  "run"

* run the example  ../src/work/t2.exe

This reads the input file events.ini, and produces the output funcs.root.  The first time program is run this produces fmultiplicity_375215AB.txt . After that the "fmultiplicity" file is read and not created. 

Another input file is blastwave.ini, which is not used at this moment (but could be)

* a plot of the output in funcs.root can be made with 

root -b -q plot_pitypes.C

which creates c1.pdf




